I should have mentioned originally that things will be a lot simpler if you are willing to replace the histogram with a rug plot. In that case all you need is

ggplot(mtc, aes(x=wt, y=mpg)) +
    geom_line(aes(y = value, color = variable), data = subset(mtc, variable == "smooth")) +
    geom_step(aes(y = value, color = variable), data = subset(mtc, variable == "step")) +

    geom_rug(sides = "b")

Best,
Ista

