Hi Anna,

See inline

On Tue, Feb 4, 2014 at 5:15 AM, Anna Zakrisson <an...@ecology.su.se> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I have a legend where some text needs to be in italics. This is no problem,
> but the justification changes when I add the italics. Why is this and how
> can I change it to be justified to the left side?
> Here is some ugly dummy data and an ugly graph. I am really bad in creating
> good dummy data. However, this script looks great for my original data. It
> illustrates my problem however. I also have problems writing parts of the
> ylab in italics. If a non-italic word is before the italics part - nothing
> is written:  ylab(expression("the", italic("y-axis italics"), "stuff"))+
> #why is this not working?
> Thank you all for your time and patience! The ggplot2 group will definitely
> be in my thesis acknowledgements! :-)
> best
> Anna
>
> mydata<- data.frame(factor1 = factor(rep(LETTERS[1:3], each = 160)), #Dummy
> data
>                     factor2 = factor(rep(c(1:2), each = 16)),
>                     factor3 = factor(rep(c(3:5), each = 32)),
>                     var1 = rnorm(120, mean = rep(c(0, 3, 15), each = 40),
>                                  sd = rep(c(1, 3, 6), each = 20)),
>                     var2 = rnorm(120, mean = rep(c(14, 35, 2), each = 40),
>                                  sd = rep(c(6, 1, 0.3), each = 20)))
>
> p <- ggplot(data = mydata,aes(x = var1,y = var2)) +
>   theme_bw()+
>   ggtitle("This is extremely ugly and unclear, but please ignore this as my
> question is
>           regarding the legend justification only. I am bad at creating good
> dummy data. Sorry.")+
>   ylab(expression("the", italic("y-axis italics"), "stuff"))+ #why is this
> not working?

you need 'expression(paste("the ", italic("y-axis italics"), "stuff")))'

>   xlab("the x-axis stuff")+
>   geom_point(mapping=aes(shape=factor2, col=factor3), size=3.5)+
>   theme(axis.text.x = element_text(size = 12, colour="black",
> family="serif", angle=90))
> p + scale_colour_discrete(name  ="my factor 3",
>                           breaks=c("3", "4", "5"),
>                           labels=c("factor 3-3", "factor 3-4", "factor
> 3-5")) +
>   scale_shape_discrete(name  ="my factor 2",
>                        breaks=c("1", "2"),
>                        labels=expression(italic("italics factor 2-1"),
>                                          "factor 2-2"))+
>   theme(legend.key = element_blank())

If you don't like the legend label alignment you can change it;

  theme(legend.key = element_blank(), legend.text.align = 0)

see ?theme for the list of things you can change.

Best,
Ista

