In-Reply-To: <OAnVYgR61wE.1rvjzch_d9YJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <OAnVYgR61wE.1rvjzch_d9YJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/OAnVYgR61wE/m/2Pi9uyOuZqYJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Would geom_tile do what you want?

Eg:

# convert the times to named lists so we can get at the hour and day separately
data4$hfac = as.POSIXlt(data4$hfac)

ggplot(data=data4, aes(x=hfac$hour, y=hfac$yday, fill=H)) + geom_tile() + scale_fill_gradient(low="green", high="red")

Malcolm

